Reused excerpts and changes (Apache-2.0 section 4(b) change notes):

1. Schema and entity definitions (node labels, relationship types, property
   names and key properties for Vulnerability, Exploit, Author, Weakness,
   Product, Vendor, Domain).
   Changes: CVSS score properties are stored as decimals (VulKG casts several
   to integers); no range index on Vulnerability.description (a full-text
   index is used instead).

2. Load steps adapted from 2.VulKG_Deployment_Cypher.cypher (load order and
   MERGE semantics).
   Changes:
   - Rewritten in Neo4j 5.26 syntax (constraints, indexes, SHOW commands).
   - Loaded by a Go loader over Bolt instead of apoc.load.csv and
     apoc.periodic.iterate.
   - affectedVersion is replaced on each load instead of appended.
   - CVSS scores are decimals.
   - No description range index.

3. The pinned VulKG import CSV files are not stored in this repository. They
   are fetched from an operator-controlled S3 bucket and verified by SHA-256.

Excluded from this repository: VulKG machine-learning scripts, datasets, and
embedding artifacts.
